{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSTnUDcdN2AdiNPdaCU6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings (paths and line numbers):**\n- Shipment data class: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27`\n- ShipmentStatus enum: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:23-27`\n- ShipmentController (no confirm endpoint today): `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20-56`\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository.save(): `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:15-18`\n- ConflictException: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:22-24`\n- ResourceNotFoundException: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:18-20`\n- ErrorCode enum: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37`\n- GlobalExceptionHandler: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28`\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Controllers throw domain-specific `ApiException` subclasses; `GlobalExceptionHandler` translates them to HTTP responses with `ApiError` envelope\n- `ConflictException(ErrorCode.X, message)` for 409 responses; `ResourceNotFoundException(ErrorCode.Y, message)` for 404\n- ErrorCode enum is the authoritative set of error scenarios—each must have an entry\n- POST endpoints that create/mutate resources return the affected entity in the response body\n- Tests use `MockMvc` with `jsonPath()` to verify response structure; `@BeforeEach` resets the repository\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — must add a new `confirm` handler; this cannot be avoided\n2. `ApiError.kt` — must add a new ErrorCode for the \"shipment in invalid status for confirm\" scenario; required to match the error contract pattern\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for the four cases (success, idempotent success, cancelled rejection, not-found rejection); required to verify the feature\n\n**Risks:**\n- The new ErrorCode enum entry is a public API change (clients depend on the set of codes)\n- Idempotency: confirming an already-confirmed shipment must succeed and persist, which could mask application bugs if the repository were transactional\n- The confirm endpoint returns the shipment, but if serialization changed, clients might reject it\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone. The ticket is clear on all cases and status codes.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to the ErrorCode enum to represent the case where a shipment cannot be confirmed because it is in `CANCELLED` state. This maintains the pattern of having a specific code for each error scenario.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new handler method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` decorated with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`:\n   - Fetch the shipment by ID; throw `ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, ...)` if it does not exist\n   - Check the current status:\n     - If `CREATED`: transition to `CONFIRMED`, save, and return the saved shipment\n     - If `CONFIRMED`: save (no-op update) and return the saved shipment (idempotent)\n     - If `CANCELLED`: throw `ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS, ...)`\n   - Return 200 OK with the shipment in the response body\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test cases:\n   - `confirms a created shipment`: create a shipment, confirm it, verify status is now `CONFIRMED` and response is 200 OK\n   - `idempotently confirms a confirmed shipment`: create, confirm, confirm again, verify second confirm succeeds with no change\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409`: manually insert a `CANCELLED` shipment into the repository, attempt to confirm, verify 409 with error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS`\n   - `rejects confirming an unknown shipment with 404`: attempt to confirm a non-existent ID, verify 404 with error code `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`\n\n**Alternative considered:**\n- Could add a service layer between controller and repository to encapsulate the state-transition logic. This was rejected because the existing codebase has no service layer—controllers use the repository directly. Introducing one would be unrelated refactoring and violate the constraint \"Do not modify files outside the shipment feature, except tests if required.\"\n- Could use a single generic error code like `VALIDATION_FAILED` for the cancelled case. This was rejected because the existing pattern is to use specific error codes (e.g., `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` for the duplicate case), and the ticket requires \"error responses consistent with the rest of this API.\"\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Operation | Output | HTTP | Error Code |\n|------|-------|-----------|--------|------|------------|\n| Normal confirm | CREATED shipment ID | Fetch, transition to CONFIRMED, save | Shipment (CONFIRMED status) | 200 OK | — |\n| Idempotent confirm | CONFIRMED shipment ID | Fetch, no-op save (status unchanged) | Shipment (CONFIRMED status) | 200 OK | — |\n| Cancelled rejection | CANCELLED shipment ID | Fetch, detect CANCELLED, throw | Error envelope | 409 Conflict | SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS |\n| Not found | Non-existent ID | Fetch fails, throw | Error envelope | 404 Not Found | SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- **Test 1** (`confirms a created shipment`): Covers the happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED transition, persistence, response). Verifies the primary acceptance criterion.\n- **Test 2** (`idempotently confirms a confirmed shipment`): Covers idempotency by confirming twice and verifying the second call succeeds without error and status remains CONFIRMED. Addresses the \"retry must not fail\" requirement.\n- **Test 3** (`rejects confirming a cancelled shipment`): Covers the error case by manually inserting a CANCELLED shipment and attempting to confirm. Verifies the 409 response with the correct error code.\n- **Test 4** (`rejects confirming an unknown shipment`): Covers the 404 case by attempting to confirm a non-existent ID. Verifies the error code matches `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`.\n\nAll four tests together verify acceptance criteria 1–7 (existing build/tests pass, endpoint exists, persistence works, errors are consistent, idempotency works, no new dependencies, no unrelated changes).\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Starting with ApiError.kt to add the new ErrorCode:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":407,"cache_read_input_tokens":20238,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":407},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65879cc5-bc3d-46d9-bae6-1b1a7acf45bc","uuid":"1bee02a7-dcfa-4895-a7f3-0dec71d2ed73","timestamp":"2026-09-26T17:41:59.154Z","request_id":"req_011CfSTnTqYhoswbfU7YmBcU"}
