{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSTsBPU3PpJ4gWkK44YG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests pass: 17 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors. The ShipmentControllerTest shows 9 tests (5 existing + 4 new) all passing.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. **Existing build passes** → BUILD SUCCESS reported in verification\n2. **Existing tests pass** → All 5 original ShipmentControllerTest tests still pass; 4 tests in OrderControllerTest and 3 in CustomerControllerTest pass\n3. **`POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` confirms a created shipment and persists it** → Test \"confirms a created shipment\" verifies this; checks status becomes CONFIRMED and response code is 200\n4. **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** → Uses existing `ConflictException` and `ResourceNotFoundException` patterns; error code added to existing `ErrorCode` enum; `GlobalExceptionHandler` already handles the new error codes\n5. **A repeated confirm succeeds; a cancelled shipment is refused; an unknown id is refused** → Three separate tests cover these:\n   - \"idempotently confirms a confirmed shipment\" — confirms twice, both succeed with 200\n   - \"rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409\" — returns 409 Conflict with `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` code\n   - \"rejects confirming an unknown shipment with 404\" — returns 404 Not Found with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` code\n6. **No new Maven dependency appears** → pom.xml untouched\n7. **No unrelated production file changes** → Only ShipmentController.kt and ApiError.kt modified; both are in the shipment feature scope\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** (necessary change) — Added `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to ErrorCode enum. This is the minimal addition required to represent the error case per the API contract pattern.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** (necessary change) — Added `confirm` handler method:\n   - Decorated with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`\n   - Fetches shipment; throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if not found\n   - Uses a `when` expression to handle three cases: CREATED (transition + save), CONFIRMED (save unchanged for idempotency), CANCELLED (throw ConflictException)\n   - Returns the saved shipment with status 200 OK (implicit from Spring)\n   - No imports added; uses only existing exception and data types\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** (necessary change) — Added four test methods:\n   - \"confirms a created shipment\" — verifies CREATED → CONFIRMED transition and response structure\n   - \"idempotently confirms a confirmed shipment\" — verifies second confirm succeeds without error\n   - \"rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409\" — verifies 409 Conflict response with correct error code\n   - \"rejects confirming an unknown shipment with 404\" — verifies 404 Not Found response with correct error code\n   - Each test verifies both HTTP status and response body (jsonPath assertions match existing test style)\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\nNone. The implementation is complete and all criteria are satisfied.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\n**Requirement:** Add a POST endpoint at `/shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that transitions a shipment from `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED` status, succeeds idempotently on already-confirmed shipments, and rejects cancelled or non-existent shipments with appropriate HTTP codes.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt` — Added `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` error code to represent the case when confirming a cancelled shipment\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` — Added `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId)` handler to perform the state transition, handle idempotency, and reject invalid cases\n- `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Added four test methods covering normal confirmation, idempotency, cancelled rejection, and not-found rejection\n\n**Tests:**\n- \"confirms a created shipment\" — Verifies that confirming a CREATED shipment transitions it to CONFIRMED and returns 200 OK with the updated shipment\n- \"idempotently confirms a confirmed shipment\" — Verifies that confirming an already-CONFIRMED shipment succeeds (no error) and status remains unchanged\n- \"rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409\" — Verifies that attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 Conflict with `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` error code\n- \"rejects confirming an unknown shipment with 404\" — Verifies that confirming a non-existent shipment ID returns 404 Not Found with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` error code\n\n**Verification:** Ran `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/` directory. Result: BUILD SUCCESS. All 17 tests passed (4 OrderControllerTest, 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests, 9 ShipmentControllerTest including 4 new, 3 CustomerControllerTest).\n\n**Not done:** Nothing. All acceptance criteria met, all tests passing, no forbidden files modified, no new dependencies added."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3389,"cache_read_input_tokens":27506,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3389},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65879cc5-bc3d-46d9-bae6-1b1a7acf45bc","uuid":"354d9623-834f-4a15-9177-992f4bf4c011","timestamp":"2026-09-26T17:42:51.350Z","request_id":"req_011CfSTsApV1UwZWoged4yKz"}
